Y2π

Y2π renders web interfaces directly from Markdown. It uses a Canvas/WebGL framebuffer for pixel‑perfect output, 
and separates layout, themes, and actions into independent layers. The engine handles bitmap fonts, input events, 
and custom animations, scripts, embeddings), covering the full webview workflow from document structure to interactive behavior. 
Everything runs on ES5 for broad compatibility.

Write your page in Markdown, configure rendering, input, and actions — the rest is up to you.
